# Keep the monorepo out of the Drupal image.
#
# package/Dockerfile does `COPY . /opt/drupal/app`, so without this file the whole
# repo lands in the image: the deployed container currently carries docs/ (2.1M),
# mkdocs/, scripts/, s3-sync/ and solr-proxy/, none of which the running app reads.
# solr-proxy/ in particular is a SEPARATE container with its own Dockerfile — it has
# no business inside the Drupal image.
#
# Only two things in the build context are actually needed:
#   drupal/  — the Composer project (composer.json), the webroot, and config/sync
#   package/ — package/data/files/.../000-default.conf, copied explicitly at line 46
#
# Verified before excluding: drupal/composer.json declares no `path` repositories and
# nothing under drupal/ symlinks outside it, so Composer never reaches up out of the
# subdirectory.
#
# See docs/deferred/pipeline-triggers-on-every-monorepo-commit.md — the same monorepo
# shape drives the missing trigger_paths filter on the pipeline.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.ddev
.claude

docs
mkdocs
mkdocs.yml

scripts
s3-sync
solr-proxy
